Visual acceptance criteria

When the work is finished:

Desert should look like a compact dimensional desert fighting platform surrounded by open space, with no enclosing cliff walls.

City should look like a compact dimensional rooftop/platform-fighter stage surrounded by open space, with no giant boundary buildings acting as walls.

Practice Ground should retain its clean one-point-perspective training-room identity but have open left/right stage edges rather than side walls.

All three stages should visibly read as smaller arenas.

The camera should be noticeably farther out than before.

Players should be able to leave the stage and fall into open space.

The black, wavy Void should exist far outside the main platform and act as the actual kill boundary.

The game should feel like it has taken its first structural step from a traditional enclosed fighting arena toward a platform fighter.

